Aim:-
b. Write a program to implement Matplotlib and Pandas libraries in python

Algorithm:-
1. Start
2. Import Libraries
    . Import Pandas library as pd
    . Import Matplotlib pyplot module as plt
3. Create Data
    . Define a dictionary with:
       . Key "teams" and values ["csk", "mi", "kkr", "rcb"]
       . Key "runs" and values [190, 150, 200, 170]
4. Create DataFrame
    . Convert the dictionary into a DataFrame using pd.DataFrame()
    . Store it in variable df
5. Display Data
    . Print the DataFrame
6. Plot Bar Graph
    . Use plt.bar() to create a bar chart
       . X-axis: df["teams"]
       . Y-axis: df["runs"]
7. Add Labels and Title
    . Set X-axis label using plt.xlabel("teams")
    . Set Y-axis label using plt.ylabel("runs")
    . Set title using plt.title("IPL Team Runs")
8. Display Graph
    . Use plt.show() to display the bar chart
9. Stop

Code:-
import pandas as pd
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt

df = pd.DataFrame({
    "teams": ["csk", "mi", "kkr", "rcb"],
    "runs": [190, 150, 200, 170]
})

print(df)

plt.bar(df["teams"], df["runs"])
plt.xlabel("teams")
plt.ylabel("runs")
plt.title("IPL Team Runs")
plt.show()

